# Theme color utilities

Brand colors live in `src/style.css` (`:root` + `@theme`). Use Tailwind theme utilities — never arbitrary `[var(--token)]` classes.

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
<div class="border-[var(--forest)] text-[var(--mint)] bg-[var(--hero)]" />
<div class="border-[var(--forest)]/10" />

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
<div class="border-forest text-mint bg-hero" />
<div class="border-forest/10" />
```

## Tokens → utilities

| CSS var | Utilities |
| --- | --- |
| `--forest` | `text-forest`, `bg-forest`, `border-forest` |
| `--paper` | `text-paper`, `bg-paper`, `border-paper` |
| `--sage` | `text-sage`, `bg-sage`, `border-sage` |
| `--mist` | `text-mist`, `bg-mist`, `border-mist` |
| `--moss` | `text-moss`, `bg-moss`, `border-moss` |
| `--mint` | `text-mint`, `bg-mint`, `border-mint` |
| `--leaf` | `text-leaf`, `bg-leaf`, `border-leaf` |
| `--hero` | `text-hero`, `bg-hero`, `border-hero` |
| `--hero-elevated` | `text-hero-elevated`, `bg-hero-elevated`, `border-hero-elevated` |
| `--ink` | `text-ink`, `bg-ink`, `border-ink` |

Opacity modifiers work the same way: `border-forest/20`, `bg-mint/15`.

If a color token is missing from `@theme`, add it there — do not fall back to `[var(--…)]`.
